## WebSocket Events (Real-time Notifications)
The notification system supports real-time updates via Socket.IO. Users automatically join their personal notification room upon connection.

### Client Events (emit to server):
- **join-notifications** - Explicitly join notification room (automatic on connection)
- **leave-notifications** - Leave notification room

### Server Events (listen on client):
- **new-notification** - New notification received
  - Data: `{ notification_id, title, message, entity_type, notification_type, created_at }`
- **notification-read** - Notification marked as read
  - Data: `{ notification_id }`
- **notification-deleted** - Notification deleted
  - Data: `{ notification_id }`
- **all-notifications-read** - All notifications marked as read
  - Data: `{ updated_count }`
- **todo-completed** - Todo marked as completed
  - Data: `{ notification_id }`
- **todo-incomplete** - Todo marked as incomplete
  - Data: `{ notification_id }`
- **unread-count** - Unread notification count updated
  - Data: `{ count }`
- **joined-notifications** - Confirmation of joining notification room
  - Data: `{ room }`

### Notification System Features
- **Entity-based notifications**: Subscribe to notifications for any entity type (initiatives, projects, NCRs, etc.)
- **Subscription management**: Users can subscribe/unsubscribe to specific entities
- **Notification preferences**: JSON-based preferences for customizing notification delivery
- **Read/unread tracking**: Track which notifications have been read by each user
- **Email tracking**: Track email delivery status for notifications
- **Bulk operations**: Mark all notifications as read, get unread counts
- **Helper endpoints**: Convenient endpoints for common notification types (created, updated, status changed)
- **Role-based access**: Different permissions for creating vs. consuming notifications
- **Real-time WebSocket support**: Live notification updates via Socket.IO for instant user feedback

